WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.850
Lucía texts a friend from a campsite.

2
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:06.450
In English, every line
would use "am" or "is".

3
00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:07.770
"I am hungry.

4
00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:08.850
" "It is sunny.

5
00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:10.150
" "I am writing.

6
00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:14.076
" But her Spanish uses three
different verbs: Tengo hambre.

7
00:00:14.126 --> 00:00:15.333
Hace sol.

8
00:00:15.383 --> 00:00:16.590
Estoy escribiendo.

9
00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:20.250
So how do you know which
verb each sentence needs?

10
00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:23.330
In this mission, you'll build
a two-word tense for what's

11
00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:26.770
happening right now, and
learn when not to use it.

12
00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:30.410
You'll also meet three everyday
patterns that take jobs English

13
00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:34.010
gives to "to be": tener, hay, hace.

14
00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:38.190
Your mission: pick the right
verb for every line of Lucía's

15
00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:39.220
text.
